    "7": "A borrowed word frequently retains a phonological shape that violates the receiving language's historical sound laws.",
    "8": "Linguists test a shared item by reconstructing a proto-language form and checking whether both languages' forms follow from it by known sound laws.",
    "9": "The term Sprachbund designates a set of geographically contiguous languages that share structural features without descending from a recent common ancestor.",
    "10": "Albanian, Romanian, and Bulgarian each belong to a different branch of Indo-European.",
    "11": "Albanian, Romanian, and Bulgarian all place the definite article after the noun.",
    "12": "The languages of the Balkan Sprachbund all descend from a single Indo-European branch called Paleo-Balkan.",
    "13": "Documented historical bilingualism between two speech communities supports a contact explanation for a shared feature."
}

print(json.dumps(recover_relations(response, atoms), indent=4))
